# Cast for the Mermaid Sequence
#
# Three caricatures from a real-world ed-tech argument. Used by the Chat
# blocks in MermaidSequence.olx.

Piotr:
  seed: piotr_eastern_european
  openPeeps:
    face: blank
    head: medium3
    facialHair: full
    skinColor: f8d5c2
    clothingColor: '264653'
    headContrastColor: d6b370
  profile:
    role: Ed-tech researcher and entrepreneur
    bio: |
      Eastern European. Speaks in declarative sentences that end before
      you expect them to. Will tell you your code is wrong, your
      architecture is wrong, and possibly your worldview is wrong, all
      in the same breath, and he'll be right about at least two of them.
      Has strong opinions about strictness, both in type systems and in
      life. Believes "this is fine" is a load-bearing lie. Drinks his
      coffee black and his feedback blacker. Anyone and everyone can and
      should achieve excellence if they just work harder and push harder.
      And when they do that? Raise the bar for excellence. He built this
      platform... and several others. It's HIS platform.

John:
  seed: john_reading_researcher
  openPeeps:
    face: contempt
    head: short2
    facialHair: chin
    skinColor: f8d5c2
    clothingColor: 6c757d
    headContrastColor: e8e1e1
  profile:
    role: Reading Researcher
    bio: |
      Speaks slowly, the way one does when the other party is clearly
      going to need the extra time. Begins sentences with "Well,
      actually..." and somehow makes it land. Has read the paper you're
      about to cite, and also the paper that paper was wrong about.
      Smiles benevolently when corrected, then corrects you back twice
      as hard, twenty minutes later, in writing, with citations. After
      decades of experience studying the topic, he no longer believes
      people can learn. Himself included. Or do much of anything else.
      Leading this grant... and many others. It's HIS project.

Omer:
  seed: omer_kindly_prof
  openPeeps:
    face: explaining
    head: short5
    skinColor: ffd5b2
    headContrastColor: 2c1b18
  profile:
    role: Kindly Professor
    bio: |
      The kindly professor who genuinely just wants everyone to learn
      something today. Walks into the meeting with a thoughtful question
      about reading comprehension and walks out having mediated a treaty
      between two ed-research factions who didn't realize they'd been
      fighting. Says "that's a really interesting point" and means it
      both times. Will gently rephrase Piotr's most cutting remark as
      "what I think Piotr is getting at is..." and somehow make Piotr
      nod. Teaching this class. It's HIS class and HIS students.
